WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.830
A young teacher proudly showed me her unit

2
00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:06.010
plan: a new AI tool every lesson.

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.420
I asked: what should the pupils learn?

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.180
Today: design a unit where AI

5
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.580
serves the learning.

6
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.640
Plan backwards.

7
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.600
Start with the goals: what pupils

8
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.480
should know and do by the end.

9
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.220
Then the evidence: how you’ll

10
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.100
know they got there.

11
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:26.650
Then the activities.

12
00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.030
Only then ask where AI could help.

13
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.230
For each activity, AI has three places.

14
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.960
It can help you, drafting questions or

15
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.620
simpler texts that you check.

16
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.160
Pupils can use it, with a set AI level.

17
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.870
Or it stays out, where the

18
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.190
struggle is the learning.

19
00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.320
Two rules for every plan.

20
00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:53.810
Each AI activity has a no-device

21
00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:56.230
path: a printout, one phone per

22
00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.670
group, or a demonstration.

23
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.040
And everything AI makes is checked

24
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.900
for facts, level, bias and local

25
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.720
fit before pupils see it.

26
00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.240
So an AI-supported unit starts from goals,

27
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.760
uses AI only where it helps, includes

28
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.560
every pupil, and keeps a person checking.

29
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.820
AI is a tool in the plan, not the plan.

30
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.530
It’s like a pressure cooker.

31
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.760
It saves hours on beans, but

32
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.760
nobody makes a salad in it.

33
00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:31.730
You plan the meal first, then use

34
00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:32.790
the cooker where it helps.

35
00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:34.590
Quick check!

36
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.220
When should AI stay out of a lesson?

37
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.700
When the struggle is the learning.

38
00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:43.900
If the goal is writing an

39
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.880
argument, pupils write it.

40
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.960
If it’s reading a rainfall graph,

41
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.500
they read it themselves.

42
00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.770
AI can come in afterwards,

43
00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:53.030
to give feedback.

44
00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.430
Here’s a three-week

45
00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:56.830
science unit on floods.

46
00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.710
AI drafts the teacher’s rainfall

47
00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:02.550
worksheets at three levels, and she checks

48
00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:02.770
them.

49
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:06.030
Groups ask a chatbot on one phone for

50
00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.390
flood-safety tips and check them

51
00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:09.810
against the official leaflet.

52
00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.650
AI stays out of their rain-gauge

53
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.510
readings and interviews with elders.

54
00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.130
Then judge the unit.

55
00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.960
Give a short quiz before and after, look

56
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.420
at pupils’ work, and ask their views.

57
00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:25.990
Share what worked, and what

58
00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.270
didn’t, at a staff meeting.

59
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.020
That’s how a whole school learns.

60
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.340
In the app, fourteen days of weather show

61
00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.200
when a class played football at break.

62
00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.540
Build a decision tree, one question at a

63
00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.660
time, or let the computer pick.

64
00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.660
You see exactly why it decides,

65
00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.560
so pupils can question it.

66
00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.230
Your turn.

67
00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.340
Half my class has no phone at home.

68
00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.780
How should my unit use AI?

69
00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:58.350
AI work in class, in groups, with a

70
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:01.130
paper path, so no pupil is left out.

71
00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:05.050
Remember: goals first, AI only where

72
00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.390
it helps, everything checked, and

73
00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:08.970
the unit judged and shared.

74
00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.090
Try it in class tomorrow: a

75
00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.910
“Decision tree from our data”.

76
00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:16.330
The class lists the last ten

77
00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.490
school days: the weather, and

78
00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:19.470
whether they played outside.

79
00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.560
Together, build a tree of

80
00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.440
yes-or-no questions on the board.

81
00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.370
Then ask: where would our tree go wrong?
